{"kind":"assert","text":"The public externally-signed append boundary requires one kernel-package decision, so implementation is stopped before commit. An outside actor must sign the exact bytes that internal/intent.Sign and Verify bind to the unexported domainTag. The current WIP can prepare and verify the canonical intent, but making the signer reproduce gitseq.intent.v0 NUL in host would duplicate kernel protocol meaning across the boundary. The narrow alternative is for internal/intent to expose one canonical signing-bytes function that validates the encoded intent and prepends its owned domain. That changes the kernel package surface even though it changes no encoding or sequencing semantics. Condition (4) says to stop and file this finding rather than make that change. The public-host worktree is preserved uncommitted; no kernel file, commit, artifact, review, or push was made."}